{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/458411-advice-for-one-on-one-game","id":458411,"title":"Advice for One-On-One Game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-26T15:52:37-07:00","id":458411,"title":"Advice for One-On-One Game","content":"I am converting a game from a group session to a one-on-one game with my girlfriend. Thanks to schedules everyone else is unable to attend so it is now a single person game. I am looking for general advice or mechanics that would fit nicely for single person games.<br /> <br /> Currently speaking as it stands:<ul><li><b>Player: </b>Mekhet (is a Hollow but she doesn't know that)</li> <li><b>Sire:</b> Murdered and then embraced her to try and replicate his own murder and embrace. She has Dream Vision (having watched her with auspex for weeks) and hopes to use that connection to pierce the veil of history and see the truth.</li> <li><b>Childe: </b>The sire has two childe's along with the player. One is essentially a Daeva in a Mekhet's disguise more focused on elysiums. The other was a member of the Paris Commune and still seeks political change.</li> </ul><ul><li><b>City:</b> New Orleans in 2007, it is two years since Katrina hit the city.</li> <li><b>Politics: </b>The city is ruled by a Lancea Sanctum Archbishop Nosferatu who rules through spies and fear. Instead of other covenants it is primarily various powerful Elysiums garnering influence.</li> <li><b>Plot: </b>While plot is somewhat undeveloped now; I want to focus on the personal side of things and the night-to-night issues of kindred.</li> </ul>A couple twists in my world that could be plot points as well. Anyone who can see ghosts can spot any old Kindred almost immediately for they tend to harbour many ghosts around them; victims of past crimes. This has led to Kindred who can speak to ghosts having a disproportionate amount of influence. Strix operate differently as well they form through acts of debauchery that the Kindred has done and seek to torment their creator but are easily distracted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2504,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2504-fallen-seraph","user":"Fallen Seraph","date":". 03-26-2015, 06:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2504-fallen-seraph","name":"Fallen Seraph","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T16:17:10-07:00","id":458456,"title":"","content":"I love these sort of games for how much freedom they allow in exploring ones character with no burden of those other PCs who don't care <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> And that's probably my only advise: Remember, you're not forcing anyone to wait if you go on a two hour debate about politics which circles around most of the time if the two of you are having fun <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> nobody's forced to listen to tat circling stuff so knock yourself out.<br /> <br /> As for mechanics, it completely depends on how you want to run the game... you could keep them even to a minimum.<br /> <br /> Anyways, whatever happens, do keep the forums updated <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T16:22:01-07:00","id":458479,"title":"","content":"Currently speaking what has happened:<ul><li>Has had a couple weeks of getting to understand being a vamp.</li> <li>She understood how public feeding can bite you in the ass as a hungry ghoul followed her home and tried to feed on her during the day. Caused her first death and humanity drop (happened on Sunday during the day so took the Holy Day bane).</li> <li>Starting to notice mirrors acting weird, and discovered a rat has been eaten in her apartment.</li> <li>She has met a Nosferatu who is slowly bringing her into a web of favours. He acts like a cool 50's ratpack guy but uses neonates for most of his activities. He does have upsides. He can dispose of bodies easily enough; brings his own chevy to your place chuck the body in the trunk and the rats there feast.</li> <li>Had a friend/beginning of a blood doll get taken in a club by another Kindred. Doesn't know what happened to her.</li> </ul>Her current long-term aspirations (haven't figured out short ones yet):<ul><li>Create a piece of art that describes the vampire experience to her.</li> <li>Find a family in this new life.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2504,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2504-fallen-seraph","user":"Fallen Seraph","date":". 03-26-2015, 07:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2504-fallen-seraph","name":"Fallen Seraph","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}